[agent] ## Summary
[agent] I built the full FTI fraud-detection pipeline entirely **on the Hopsworks platform** (CLI-only mode — local Python/ML is blocked, so all compute ran server-side via a `hops job`).
[agent] **Approach:** Uploaded the two CSVs to HopsFS, then deployed one Python pipeline as a platform job (`pandas-training-pipeline` env) that did all the real work server-side: feature engineering, feature-store writes, training-dataset materialization, model training/registration, and scoring.
[agent] **Deliverables (all verified via CLI):**
[agent] | Artifact | Status |
[agent] |---|---|
[agent] | **Feature group `cctxn18c7ed`** | 24,111 rows, engineered features: geo-distance from card centroid (haversine), amount z-score/ratio vs card mean, transaction velocity (secs-since-prev, count-in-1h), hour/day-of-week, log-amount, category. `event_time=datetime`, PK `transaction_id`. |
[agent] | **Feature view + training dataset `cctd18c7ed`** | v1, label `is_fraud`, 80/20 train/test split materialized point-in-time-correct. |
[agent] | **Model `ccmodel18c7ed`** | HistGradientBoosting classifier, registered with metrics `roc_auc=0.99998, accuracy=0.9990, f1=0.9721`. |
[agent] | **Predictions `ccpred18c7ed`** | 5,293 rows (every score row), PK `transaction_id`, `fraud_probability` ∈ [0,1]. **Online=yes** — enabled for low-latency lookup alongside offline. |
[agent] **Held-out ROC AUC ≈ 1.000**, far above the 0.742 pass threshold (the geo-distance and amount-anomaly features are extremely discriminative on this data).
[agent] One CLI note: `hops td list` errored with `_get_training_dataset_schema` — a client/backend version mismatch (CLI 5.1.0.dev1 vs backend 5.0.0), not a data problem. The TD's existence is confirmed by the job log (`training dataset version 1`) and `hops fv info`.
